  "title": "Arban – Major Scales No. 35",
  "lead": "From Arban's Grande méthode complète de cornet à pistons et de saxhorn, first edition, 1864. The notes are the cornet part as printed, in written pitch for the B♭ cornet. Below: the book's own words, translated from the French.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Book",
    "Arban, Grande méthode complète de cornet à pistons et de saxhorn, first edition (Paris: Léon Escudier, 1864)"
   ],
   [
    "Section",
    "Major Scales"
   ],
   [
    "Page in the book",
    "66"
   ]
  ],
  "sections": [
   {
    "heading": "Major scales",
    "paragraphs": [
     "The study of scales has always been much neglected in works of this kind. Most of them give a few examples and leave the pupil to find in himself whatever the method leaves out. What comes of it? Very few artists know how to play a scale correctly.",
     "Yet scales must be worked at, and worked at steadily. Knowing how much this kind of study matters, I have treated this part at great length, and in every key. This work gives a perfectly even sound, and playing that is smooth and correct."
    ]
   }
  ],
